# Clp's dependency chain, in build order, pinned exactly like the solvers.
#
# Clp does not stand alone: it needs CoinUtils for its data structures and Osi
# for the solver interface it implements. Those are libraries, not competitors,
# so they live here rather than in solvers.manifest — the loop there builds a
# binary and runs it, and neither of these is one.
#
# Same format: a data line, then the url on the line after it. Same rules —
# the sha256 is the one that was actually downloaded, and the licence is
# verified at fetch time rather than trusted.
#
# Versions are the ones contemporaneous with Clp 1.17.11. A newer CoinUtils is
# not automatically compatible, and the point of pinning is that "the
# comparison" does not move when somebody upstream tags a release.
#
# name     version    licence   sha256 of the source archive
# url

coinutils  2.11.12    EPL-2.0   eef1785d78639b228ae2de26b334129fe6a7d399c4ac6f8fc5bb9054ba00de64
https://github.com/coin-or/CoinUtils/archive/refs/tags/releases/2.11.12.tar.gz

osi        0.108.11   EPL-2.0   1063b6a057e80222e2ede3ef0c73c0c54697e0fee1d913e2bef530310c13a670
https://github.com/coin-or/Osi/archive/refs/tags/releases/0.108.11.tar.gz
